IMPORT prelude

-- Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974 (Singapore) -- when a termination is lawful (s 3(1), (2)), who may have one (s 3(3)), the
-- limits by duration of pregnancy (s 4), the relief for drug-only treatment (s 10), the offences of contravening s 3 (s 3(4)), coercion
-- (s 5) and unauthorised disclosure (s 7), and conscientious objection (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 5/12/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/TPA1974.txt. The cover says the revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the
-- latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 19 of 2025 (wef 05/12/2025), which rewrote the definition of "approved institution"
-- by reference to the Healthcare Services Act 2020.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the Act that decides whether, where, by whom and how late in a pregnancy
-- a woman in Singapore may have a pregnancy terminated, and it protects her from being coerced and her records from being disclosed.
-- SCOPED to the provisions a woman, her doctor and the people around her meet. Not encoded: the definitions as such (s 2), the
-- inspection power (s 8), and the regulation-making power (s 11). The regulations themselves -- who is an "authorised medical
-- practitioner", the "prescribed" qualifications and period, the persons and purposes to whom disclosure is "prescribed", the form of
-- consent -- were not retrieved; each is a yes/no fact here. The Act says nothing about the consent of a minor's parent or of a
-- husband, and nothing here says otherwise.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Termination of Pregnancy Act 1974`

DECLARE Treatment HAS
    `weeks of pregnancy` IS A NUMBER
    `requested by the pregnant woman` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with her written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `by an authorised medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an approved institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `solely by drugs prescribed by an authorised medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the practitioner holds the prescribed qualifications or special skill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately necessary to save her life` IS A BOOLEAN
    `immediately necessary to prevent grave permanent injury to her physical or mental health` IS A BOOLEAN
    `she is a citizen or the wife of a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `she holds a work pass or is the wife of a holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months resident in Singapore immediately before` IS A NUMBER

§§ `3(3) -- who may have a termination`

-- s 3(3): "No treatment to terminate pregnancy may be carried out by an authorised medical practitioner unless the pregnant woman --
-- (a) is a citizen of Singapore or is the wife of a citizen of Singapore; (b) is the holder, or is the wife of a holder, of a work pass
-- issued under the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990; or (c) has been resident in Singapore for a period of at least 4 months
-- immediately preceding the date on which the treatment is to be carried out, but this subsection does not apply to any treatment to
-- terminate pregnancy which is immediately necessary to save the life of the pregnant woman."
--
-- The exception is LIFE only. Unlike s 4(1)(a) and s 6(3), it does not extend to preventing "grave permanent injury". Residence is
-- counted here in months as a number; how a part-month is counted is not said in the Act.
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A Treatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the woman is eligible under section 3(3)` IF
        `the treatment`'s `she is a citizen or the wife of a citizen`
    OR  `the treatment`'s `she holds a work pass or is the wife of a holder`
    OR  `the treatment`'s `months resident in Singapore immediately before` AT LEAST 4
    OR  `the treatment`'s `immediately necessary to save her life`

§§ `3(2) and 10 -- who and where`

-- s 3(2): "Except as provided by section 10, every treatment to terminate pregnancy must be carried out by an authorised medical
-- practitioner in an approved institution."
-- s 10: where the treatment "consists solely of the use of drugs prescribed by an authorised medical practitioner and does not,
-- therefore, include any surgical operation or procedure, it is not necessary -- (a) for the authorised medical practitioner to hold
-- the prescribed qualifications or to have acquired skill in the treatment over the prescribed period; and (b) for the treatment to
-- be carried out in an approved institution."
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A Treatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practitioner and place meet section 3(2)` IF
        `the treatment`'s `by an authorised medical practitioner`
    AND (   `the treatment`'s `in an approved institution`
         OR `the treatment`'s `solely by drugs prescribed by an authorised medical practitioner`)

§§ `4 and 10 -- duration of pregnancy`

-- s 4(1): "No treatment to terminate pregnancy may be carried out -- (a) if the pregnancy is of more than 24 weeks' duration, unless the
-- treatment is immediately necessary to save the life or to prevent grave permanent injury to the physical or mental health of the
-- pregnant woman; or (b) if the pregnancy is of more than 16 weeks' duration but less than 24 weeks' duration, unless the treatment is
-- carried out by an authorised medical practitioner who -- (i) is in possession of the prescribed surgical or obstetric
-- qualifications; or (ii) has acquired special skill in such treatment ... over the prescribed period."
-- s 4(2): duration "is calculated from the first day of the last normal menstruation ... or ... may be ascertained by clinical
-- examination".
--
-- Read literally, a pregnancy of EXACTLY 24 weeks is neither "more than 24 weeks" nor "less than 24 weeks", so neither limb applies.
-- That is encoded as written; whether s 4(2)'s "to the end of the 24th week" closes the gap is not decided here. s 10(a) removes the
-- qualification requirement of limb (b) for drug-only treatment; it does not touch limb (a).
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A Treatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duration limits of section 4 are met` IF
    IF `the treatment`'s `weeks of pregnancy` GREATER THAN 24
    THEN    `the treatment`'s `immediately necessary to save her life`
         OR `the treatment`'s `immediately necessary to prevent grave permanent injury to her physical or mental health`
    ELSE IF     `the treatment`'s `weeks of pregnancy` GREATER THAN 16
            AND `the treatment`'s `weeks of pregnancy` LESS THAN 24
         THEN    `the treatment`'s `the practitioner holds the prescribed qualifications or special skill`
              OR `the treatment`'s `solely by drugs prescribed by an authorised medical practitioner`
         ELSE TRUE

§§ `3(1) -- protection from the law relating to abortion`

-- s 3(1): "Subject to the provisions of this Act, a person shall not be guilty of an offence under the law relating to abortion when a
-- pregnancy is terminated by an authorised medical practitioner acting on the request of a pregnant woman and with her written
-- consent." s 2: "law relating to abortion" means ss 312 to 315 of the Penal Code 1871.
--
-- Reading "Subject to the provisions of this Act" as requiring compliance with s 3(2), s 3(3) and s 4 is an INFERENCE; the Act does
-- not say in terms what happens to the protection when s 4 is breached.
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A Treatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the termination is protected from the abortion offences` IF
        `the treatment`'s `requested by the pregnant woman`
    AND `the treatment`'s `with her written consent`
    AND `the practitioner and place meet section 3(2)` `the treatment`
    AND `the woman is eligible under section 3(3)` `the treatment`
    AND `the duration limits of section 4 are met` `the treatment`

§§ `3(4) -- contravening section 3`

-- s 3(4): "Any person who contravenes or fails to comply with this section shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $3,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both."
--
-- s 4 has no penalty clause of its own, and s 3(4) reaches only "this section". So a termination by an authorised practitioner in an
-- approved institution at 30 weeks, without necessity, is NOT a s 3(4) offence; it falls outside s 3(1) and back under the Penal Code
-- (an inference, as above). Treating s 3(1) (request and written consent) as a condition of protection rather than a duty that can be
-- "contravened" is also a reading of the text; only s 3(2) and (3) are treated as contravenable here.
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A Treatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 is contravened` IF
        (NOT (`the practitioner and place meet section 3(2)` `the treatment`))
    OR  (NOT (`the woman is eligible under section 3(3)` `the treatment`))

§§ `5 -- coercion or intimidation`

-- s 5: "Any person who, by means of coercion or intimidation, compels or induces a pregnant woman against her will to undergo treatment
-- to terminate pregnancy shall be guilty of an offence" -- $3,000 or 3 years or both.
GIVEN `used coercion or intimidation` IS A BOOLEAN, `compelled or induced her against her will to undergo treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the coercion offence is committed` IF
    `used coercion or intimidation` AND `compelled or induced her against her will to undergo treatment`

§§ `6 -- conscientious objection`

-- s 6(1): "no person is under any duty, whether by contract or by any statutory or legal requirement, to participate in any treatment
-- to terminate pregnancy ... to which the person has a conscientious objection." (2) the burden of proof is on the objector and "may be
-- discharged by that person testifying on oath or affirmation". (3) nothing in (1) "affects any duty to participate in any treatment
-- which is immediately necessary to save the life or to prevent grave permanent injury to the physical or mental health of a pregnant
-- woman."
GIVEN `has a conscientious objection` IS A BOOLEAN, `the treatment is immediately necessary to save life or prevent grave injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may decline to participate` IF
    `has a conscientious objection` AND (NOT `the treatment is immediately necessary to save life or prevent grave injury`)

§§ `7 -- disclosure`

-- s 7(1): a person who "(a) is concerned with the keeping of medical records in connection with any treatment to terminate pregnancy;
-- or (b) participates in any treatment to terminate pregnancy, must not, unless the pregnant woman expressly consents to the
-- disclosure, disclose any facts or information relating to the treatment except to such persons and for such purposes as may be
-- prescribed." (2) $2,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `keeps the records or participated in the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN, `disclosed facts about the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the woman expressly consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `to a prescribed person for a prescribed purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
        `keeps the records or participated in the treatment`
    AND `disclosed facts about the treatment`
    AND (NOT `the woman expressly consented`)
    AND (NOT `to a prescribed person for a prescribed purpose`)

§§ `3(4), 5, 7(2) -- maximum penalties`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `contravening section 3`
    `coercion under section 5`
    `disclosure under section 7`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine in dollars` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disclosure under section 7` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 3000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `disclosure under section 7` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 36
